# Offline TS strained-cell pin notes (gpw-ts-kpoint-stress)

CP2K 2026.1 stock `PAIR_POTENTIAL TYPE` has no free-atom `TS` (only
DFTD2/D3/D3BJ/D4), so there is **no CP2K stress twin** for a multi-k
free-atom-TS run. Hard pins are **libMBD Fortran `get_ts_energy`** (git
`88069c6`) on its pure real-space lattice-sum branch
(`param%ewald_on = .false.`, `param%dipole_cutoff = 50 Å` with the ATV
Å→Bohr factor `1/0.52917720859`) — the same oracle family (and the same
binary build) as the shipped `gpw-ts-ice` / `gpw-ts-forces` /
`gpw-ts-stress` pins.

TS is **geometry-only**: \(E_{\mathrm{disp}}^{TS}\) does not depend on the
electronic k-mesh. The multi-k GPW product path rebuilds the same
`ts_pbe(...)` at every strained cell inside `energy_fixed_P_k` as the Γ
Lagrangian does, so the strained-cell energy pins and the strain-FD
dispersion stress terms are **bit-identical** to `gpw-ts-stress`.

Geometry: the `gpw-ts-ice` water dimer, cell diag(12 Å) in Bohr, free-atom
α₀/C₆/R_vdW from libMBD `ts_vdw_params`, Fermi damping s_R = 0.94, d = 20
(PBE). Strained cells: one axis scaled by 1±h at fixed fractional
coordinates (positions scale with the axis), h = 2e-3. Electronic product
path under test: MP **1×1×2** (TR-folded) RKS-PBE GPW.

Reproduce (offline; login node, `buildenv-gcc/2026.03-mpich` module):

```
git clone https://github.com/libmbd/libmbd && cd libmbd && git checkout 88069c6
cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DENABLE_SCALAPACK_MPI=OFF \
      -DBLA_VENDOR=OpenBLAS
cmake --build build -j8
gfortran -O2 -I build/src/modules pin_ts_strain.f90 -L build/src -lmbd \
         -o pin_ts_strain
LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$LIBRARY_PATH:build/src:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH" ./pin_ts_strain
```

Pinned output (libmbd 88069c6, GCC 14.3 / OpenBLAS 0.3.32 — first recorded
2026-07-31 with `gpw-ts-stress`; geometry-only reuse for this multi-k pin
on 2026-08-01):

```
E_disp isolated             =  -5.9764872295816794E-04 Ha
E_disp unstrained           =  -6.0996307733860822E-04 Ha
E_disp x +h            =  -6.1278297256613687E-04 Ha
E_disp x -h            =  -6.0709134569744607E-04 Ha
sigma_TS_xx (FD, libMBD)  =   1.2202142278E-07 Ha/Bohr3
E_disp y +h            =  -6.0992605267944588E-04 Ha
E_disp y -h            =  -6.1000059619617259E-04 Ha
sigma_TS_yy (FD, libMBD)  =  -1.5981205691E-09 Ha/Bohr3
E_disp z +h            =  -6.0996696060335368E-04 Ha
E_disp z -h            =  -6.0995897233070745E-04 Ha
sigma_TS_zz (FD, libMBD)  =   1.7125866055E-10 Ha/Bohr3
```

Never launched at ctest time.
